# Line-ending and encoding contract.
#
# Why this matters here: the .ini files under integration/*/SEST_*/ are both
# version-controlled source AND the exact bytes tools\install-sest-packs.ps1
# copies into the game's StreamingAssets folder. The Python builders write LF.
# Without a pin, a Windows checkout (core.autocrlf=true by default in Git for
# Windows) turns them into CRLF, every rebuild then reports the whole pack as
# modified, and the installed copy stops matching the builder's output.
#
# Rules are last-match-wins: the vendored-export block at the bottom must stay
# last so it overrides the per-extension rules above it.

* text=auto eol=lf

# --- Files we author ----------------------------------------------------------
*.py     text eol=lf diff=python
*.md     text eol=lf
*.json   text eol=lf
*.txt    text eol=lf
*.ini    text eol=lf
*.csv    text eol=lf

# PowerShell is checked out CRLF (native Windows convention) but stored LF,
# so a Windows editor saving CRLF produces no diff.
*.ps1    text eol=crlf

# --- Build output -------------------------------------------------------------
# Reproduced byte-for-byte by the builders; collapsed by default in reviews.
integration/*/SEST_*/**     linguist-generated=true
docs/mod-catalog.md         linguist-generated=true
docs/load-order-full.md     linguist-generated=true
data/load-order.preview.txt linguist-generated=true

# --- Vendored upstream export (must stay last) --------------------------------
# mods-source/ is a byte-faithful mirror of the exported game and Workshop
# files: some genuinely use CRLF and 74 carry a UTF-8 BOM. Never normalize it —
# a re-export must produce a content diff, not a whitespace storm — and keep it
# out of GitHub's language statistics.
mods-source/** -text
mods-source/** linguist-vendored=true
